A note, not a condition. Nothing below changes the MIT terms above: the
software is yours to use, for anything, without asking.

That said, if you are putting derate in front of real users -- a production
deployment, a shared cluster, anything where a bad launch costs somebody
their afternoon -- please get in touch first. Open an issue or a discussion
at https://github.com/Pizzaman213/derate and say what you are building on.
There are recommendations worth having about sizing, placement and the
gateway's current lack of inbound authentication, and I would rather hand
them to you up front than read about them afterwards.
